  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q7-node",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Solve the equation $\\ln(x)+\\ln(x+2)=1$, and write your answer(s) correct to two decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=0.93$ (to two decimal places)",
      "worked": "Both logarithm arguments must be positive, so $x>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ln\\bigl(x(x+2)\\bigr)&=1\\\\x(x+2)&=e\\\\x^2+2x&=e\\\\(x+1)^2&=1+e\\\\x&=-1\\pm\\sqrt{1+e}\\end{align*}$$\nThe negative root is outside the domain, so $x=-1+\\sqrt{1+e}\\approx0.93$ to two decimal places.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 35
  },
